    "notes": [
      "Package version normalizes the upstream CMake 0.1 project version and records the exact git commit; it does not name an upstream release asset.",
      "Actual compiler SDK is official LLVM/MLIR 17.0.6-9ubuntu1; original LLVM gitlink 4592543a01609feb4b3c19e81a9d54743e15e329 remains a separate retained input.",
      "HECO and exact SEAL gitlink are built from source; LLVM/MLIR and host Clang are separately pinned official prebuilt SDKs.",
      "Base OS ABI dependencies are enumerated in HOST-ABI.json. Python 3, g++, ldd and usable libseccomp are explicit runtime prerequisites.",
      "Only small BFV transpiler experiments are qualified. Interactive mode, compiler mode, automatic cryptographic parameter selection and official full-suite coverage are not claimed.",
      "This SDK profile uses the genuine in-memory FHE-to-BFV-to-EmitC pipeline. The unchanged custom BFV diagnostic printer omits string quotes, so its snapshot is not claimed to support textual roundtrip.",
      "The manual driver sets BFV degree4096/plainmodulus65537/tc128, generates fresh keys, encrypts and decrypts actual ciphertexts; the independent Python oracle checks 36 exact lane values."
    ],
    "summary": "HECO source-built bounded transpiler profile: FHE IR to BFV/EmitC to C++, followed by an explicit manual Microsoft SEAL build and encrypted execution."
